          "content": "kit-version-source: 0.3.0 · brief-schema: 1 · updated: 2026-10-06\nIN CODE since 2026-10-03 (UI-66): every screen here is now a capture of the app with the debug access on, taken 2026-10-06 on example data.\nA variant of studio.pen: the Studio with the debug tools as drawers of a left bar. Vendored from _playground.pen at 0.3.0; the flows are at 0.4.0. Not re-vendored: these screens only use Button, Emblem and tokens, and the 0.4.0 changes (disabled Button, focus token) do not show here. Desktop only: a desk tool.\n1. PURPOSE\nEvaluate Knotty's own furniture before users do, inside the Studio people already use: a 52 px bar on the left of the whole app, shown by the debug access, with one drawer per tool. Opening something from the bench (a variant, a ficha, a case's design) switches to throwaway designs that never reach the saved one, and the way out brings the saved one back.\n2. ENTRY POINTS\nThe debug access (Konami code, Ctrl+Shift+D, the settings switch, ?debug) shows the bar on every screen, Home included. Three tools: «Banco de pruebas», «Fichas» and «Entrañas de la madera» (src/ui/debug/DebugShell.tsx).\n3. SCREENS (top → bottom, one column; captures)\nHome, the bar: the 52 px bar over Home with every drawer closed.\nFichas, the drawer over Home: the reference furniture with the home screen's sketches, two per row, its code and version under each, and how many notices it has; a search by code or name and the rooms as chips with a count.\nFichas, searching: «lib» finds by code and by name.\nA ficha open in the sandbox, findings: the chip «Taller: nada de esto se guarda» with «Salir», «Exportar ficha» and the model switch in the header, and the panel's «Hallazgos» tab.\nSandbox, drawers closed.\nBanco: the modules without an expert and the cases with one; Banco, modules reviewed.\nBanco, a case opened into its steps: «Ver qué pasó» after running one case against the simulated expert.\nBitácora: the log as a drawer.\nExportar ficha: the dialog with the two probe commands.\nSelector de modelo: the expert's chip opened.\n4. BUSINESS RULES\nThe sandbox is a state of the app, not a screen: designs live in memory and the saved one is never read or written while it is on (src/adapters/persistence/sandbox.ts). Looking at a real design's findings needs no sandbox: it only reads.\nA ficha exports only while the design is still its plan (src/ui/lab/candidate.ts); the file is for probe --diff and --adopt (docs/fichas.md), the workshop never writes the repo.\nA case reads as steps (src/ui/debug/caseDetail.ts). A warning names its pieces (named in src/application/named.ts) and its «Ver en el 3D» marks them (flag in src/ui/store/scene.ts).\nThe model is read on every call (expert() in src/composition.ts), so a change applies to the next one.\n5. COPY SOURCE\nExisting: src/ui/debug/BenchPanel.tsx and DebugPanel.tsx (Banco de pruebas, Sin experto…, Con el experto, Revisar, Correr, Todos, Entrañas de la madera, Exportar, Copiar, Limpiar, the filters and the commit note), src/ui/studio/Studio.tsx (tabs, views, Nuevo diseño), src/ports/Preferences.ts (provider descriptions, expert label), src/domain/design/validation/geometry.ts (the warning), src/application/bench/grading.ts (the checks' words).\nNEW (in code on the branch that precedes this design): Fichas · Exportar ficha and its dialog · Hallazgos · Errores · Avisos de geometría and its help · Hallazgos estructurales · Ninguno · Ver en el 3D · Quitar la marca · Ver qué pasó · Después le pide · Llamadas al experto · Taller: nada de esto se guarda · El cambio vale desde la siguiente llamada.\nNothing here is new copy any more: the bar and «Salir» are in src/ui/debug/DebugShell.tsx and src/ui/studio/statuses.tsx.\nExample data, not measured: 47 / 41 variants, the counts, the case's figures and tokens, the log's lines and times.\n6. STATES NOT DRAWN\nMobile (the bar becomes three round buttons at the bottom left and a drawer takes the full width). A ficha with notices or an invalid one in the drawer; a room without fichas and a search without matches («Ninguna ficha… tiene «…» en su código o su nombre.»); a warning marked in the 3D with «Ver en el 3D»; bench groups open; a case running.\n7. OPEN FINDINGS\nUI-66 (this variant, decided; replaces UI-65). Open: the log's own copy for the bar's tooltips; whether a third drawer is ever needed.\n8. HISTORY\n→ LOG frame, below.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
